flowchart LR
  accTitle: Tiling a product larger than the array into output tiles and K chunks
  accDescr: C, 8 by 8, splits into four N by N output tiles. The inner dimension K = 12 splits into chunks of K_MAX = 8 and 4. Each tile takes one normal run per first chunk and one accumulate run per later chunk. Example: tile C11 needs run 1 on A rows 4 to 7, k 0 to 7 and B k 0 to 7, columns 4 to 7 with a normal start, then run 2 on the k 8 to 11 chunk with accumulate high and k_len 4.

  subgraph GA["A: 8 × 12 — row blocks × K chunks"]
    direction TB
    A0["rows 0–3<br/>k 0–7"]
    A1["rows 0–3<br/>k 8–11 (k_len 4)"]
    A2["rows 4–7<br/>k 0–7"]
    A3["rows 4–7<br/>k 8–11 (k_len 4)"]
  end
  subgraph GB["B: 12 × 8 — K chunks × column blocks"]
    direction TB
    B0["k 0–7<br/>cols 0–3"]
    B1["k 0–7<br/>cols 4–7"]
    B2["k 8–11<br/>cols 0–3"]
    B3["k 8–11<br/>cols 4–7"]
  end
  subgraph GC["C: 8 × 8 — N × N output tiles"]
    direction TB
    C00["tile (0,0)"]
    C01["tile (0,1)<br/>same pattern"]
    C10["tile (1,0)<br/>same pattern"]
    C11["tile (1,1)"]
  end
  A0 -->|"run 1: normal start"| C00
  A1 -->|"run 2: accumulate"| C00
  B0 -.-> C00
  B2 -.-> C00
  A2 -->|"run 1: normal start"| C11
  A3 -->|"run 2: accumulate (k_len 4)"| C11
  B1 -.-> C11
  B3 -.-> C11

  note1["Per tile: chunk 0 runs with a normal start;<br/>every later chunk runs with accumulate high.<br/>Partial sums stay in the PEs between chunks;<br/>only the finished tile is read.<br/>Rows beyond M and columns beyond P are zero-padded."]
